{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_bdrk_knwosh66qc7ikqape5gn44xqrk4prlf6q3bpdfmenlefwgdvukda","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01UzaXSaZtnmj5PuKhoMSHhk","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"fileKey":"1lB6sFZZe3WOcgYZxebEca","description":"Read text content of Start Here and Foundations pages","code":"const out=[];\nfor (const id of ['0:1','1:2']) {\n  const p = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\n  await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(p);\n  out.push('=== '+p.name);\n  const walk=(n,d)=>{\n    let s='  '.repeat(d)+n.type+' '+n.id+' \"'+n.name+'\" '+(n.width?Math.round(n.width)+'x'+Math.round(n.height):'');\n    if(n.type==='TEXT') s+=' :: '+n.characters.replace(/\\n/g,' | ');\n    if((n.type==='RECTANGLE'||n.type==='FRAME') && n.fills && n.fills.length && n.fills[0].type==='SOLID'){const c=n.fills[0].color; s+=' fill#'+[c.r,c.g,c.b].map(v=>Math.round(v*255).toString(16).padStart(2,'0')).join('');}\n    out.push(s);\n    if(n.children) for(const c of n.children) walk(c,d+1);\n  };\n  for(const c of p.children) walk(c,0);\n}\nreturn out.join('\\n');"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8896,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8896,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33fdca80-10af-4719-bef6-cca51e068667","uuid":"038d054d-962e-4089-a5da-a4d5f2dcf068","timestamp":"2026-11-01T20:17:35.232Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01UzaXSaZtnmj5PuKhoMSHhk","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01UzaXSaZtnmj5PuKhoMSHhk","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== 00 · Start Here 设计任务\nFRAME 5:2 \"Start Here · Brief\" 1440x4777 fill#ffffff\n  FRAME 5:3 \"Header\" 1312x145\n    TEXT 5:4 \"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\" 182x19 :: LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\n    TEXT 5:5 \"SHOP.CO — fashion store website\" 1312x52 :: SHOP.CO — fashion store website\n    TEXT 5:6 \"Design a fashion e-commerce website: discover new arrivals and best sellers, filter a category, review a product and its customer reviews, and check the cart. Desktop web, 1440 wide, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\" 1312x50 :: Design a fashion e-commerce website: discover new arrivals and best sellers, filter a category, review a product and its customer reviews, and check the cart. Desktop web, 1440 wide, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\n  FRAME 5:7 \"How to work\" 1312x249\n    TEXT 5:8 \"How to work\" 147x35 :: How to work\n    TEXT 5:9 \"1. Build exactly the 4 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in page order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. 3. The brand color and the two typefaces in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii, elevation and the page grid, and apply them consistently. 4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button and a default Text Field. Design all other states, the header, the footer, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file. 5. Use the photos, the social and payment logos and the icons from 04 · Media. 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\" 1312x198 :: 1. Build exactly the 4 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. | 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in page order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. | 3. The brand color and the two typefaces in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii, elevation and the page grid, and apply them consistently. | 4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button and a default Text Field. Design all other states, the header, the footer, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file. | 5. Use the photos, the social and payment logos and the icons from 04 · Media. | 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\n  FRAME 5:10 \"Frames · goals · must include · links\" 1312x1525\n    TEXT 5:11 \"Frames · goals · must include · links\" 413x35 :: Frames · goals · must include · links\n    TEXT 5:12 \"Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\" 1312x22 :: Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\n    FRAME 5:13 \"Frame cards\" 1312x1436\n      FRAME 5:14 \"01_Home\" 644x716 fill#f7f7fa\n        TEXT 5:15 \"01_Home\" 82x26 :: 01_Home\n        TEXT 5:16 \"Goal: Get inspired and find something to buy.\" 596x20 :: Goal: Get inspired and find something to buy.\n        TEXT 5:17 \"MUST INCLUDE\" 84x16 :: MUST INCLUDE\n        TEXT 5:18 \"• Announcement bar: “Sign up and get 20% off to your first order.” ·